# speaker:Datuk John # slot:left
(Hmm... The stall isn't doing too well... Everyone is selling the same generic alien food. It barely tastes like anything.)

# speaker:Datuk John # slot:left
(The only reason my stall is satying afloat is the amount of customers I attract with my low prices... Oh, looks like some delivery driver is approaching.)

# speaker:Krab Rider # slot:right
Oi! Boss, You open ke?, you macam orang Malaysia ya? You serve Malaysian cuisine here? I damn lapar leh.

# speaker:Datuk John # slot:left
No lah bang, I would like to make Malaysian Food, but here macam no ingredients.

# speaker:Krab Rider # slot:right
Haiz... Here I thought you'd hook me up. You sell the same generic alien slop here?

# speaker:Krab Rider # slot:right
At least it's cheap. There's just no spirit. I'll take one of these lah.

# speaker:Datuk John # slot:left
(Is this what I really want? To spend my life selling cheap tasteless food?)

# speaker:Datuk John # slot:left
(I'm thankful for the aliens for taking us in but... my Malaysian spirit is asking for more. Our ancestors didn't die for this!)

# speaker:Datuk John # slot:left
(If only there was some way to get the traditional ingredients... And cultivate them here!)

# speaker:Krab Rider # slot:right
Woi boss, you gonna move ke? You suffering from cyberpsychosis? Why are you lost in thought?

# speaker:Datuk John # slot:left
Come back in a few days.

# speaker:Krab Rider # slot:right
Har? Boss! Where are you going? You tak tau Malay ke? I hungry bro!

# speaker:Datuk John # slot:left
(It's time to revisit my roots.)

# speaker:Datuk John # slot:left
Nasi Lemak... The classic Malaysian dish. To make it, I need these 5 ingredients: Rice, Egg, Coconut Milk, Sambal and the sides.
